+        // elongated word, and collapsing runs destroys its value: `II` became
+        // `i`, and `XXXII` (32) became `xi` (11). Measured: 42 of 73
+        // de-elongation hits in the corpus were this, so the rule did more
+        // harm than good without the guard. Real words made of those letters
+        // (`mill`, `civil`) resolved at the lexicon step and never arrive.
+        guard !lowered.allSatisfy({ Self.romanNumeralLetters.contains($0) }) else {
+            return nil
+        }
